- [ ] Basic TUI
- [ ] Buffer rendering: Gap buffer ([gap buffers vs ropes](https://coredumped.dev/2023/08/09/text-showdown-gap-buffers-vs-ropes/))
- [ ] UTF-8 support
- [ ] Basic buffer navigation
- [ ] Basic buffer editing
- [ ] Immediate-mode rendering: double-buffered grid of cells (frame buffers), only surgically update changed cells. See [synchronized output](https://ghostty.org/docs/help/synchronized-output)
- [ ] Modal editing and selections as primitives
    > Do what Kakoune does to disambiguate escape without a timeout
- [ ] Undo tree
- [ ] Keymaps
    - Defined as `"space x"`, `"c-x c-s"`, `"g f"`, etc.
    - Use a Trie (prefix tree)
- [ ] Use Janet for scripting
- [ ] Define motions in Janet
- [ ] Changes to a buffer wrapped in a "transaction". Allows bundling changesets for undo/redo, maybe repeat
- [ ] Integration tests
- [ ] Kitty keyboard protocol with progressive enhancement
    - Report alternate keys so keymaps match physical keys. Is it possible? Should be configurable?
- [ ] selections as primitives (anchor + cursor), multiple selections, selection -> action — like kakoune
- [ ] no select mode initially, like kakoune; add it later if needed
- [ ] Create a Discord/Zulip
- [ ] Registers
- [ ] Major/minor modes like in Emacs?
- [ ] Profiling with `core:prof/spall`, Tracy, etc.
- [ ] Builtin mode line. Rendering done in Janet, so components can be reused and reordered for customization
- [ ] `minibuffer`
    - [ ] Command interface (built on minibuffer)
    - [ ] Commands are defined in kebab-case
    - [ ] Builtin module for creating commands
    - [ ] Command completion
    - [ ] `:help` command (script-defined)
- [ ] Text properties
    - Properties are prioritized, see impls from other text editors
- [ ] `gf` motion respects optional line range (script-defined)
- [ ] tree-sitter
    - [ ] Highlighting
    - [ ] Language injections
    - [ ] Text objects
    - [ ] Indentation
    - [ ] Folding
- [ ] Builtin picker module (built on minibuffer)
- [ ] LSP
- [ ] Kitty text sizing protocol: constrain text sizing to integers > 1 and text height to multiples of the default grid size, so it works nicely with the grid and everything else in the UI
- [ ] Kitty graphics protocol with selection, yank, paste, etc.
- [ ] File watcher (`autoread`)
- [ ] Server/client architecture
- [ ] Terminal buffer implementation with `libghostty`. Should handle nested editor instances.
